.SS 2. Views into the bytes and their owner
A result can hold views into the bytes: \f[CR]std::string_view\f[R] and
\f[CR]std::span<std::byte const>\f[R].
So \f[CR]decode\f[R] always returns a \f[CR]ref<T>\f[R], which holds the
owner of the bytes.
A view in the result stays valid while the \f[CR]ref\f[R] lives.
A result with no view member holds its own copy of every value.
.PP
